[[0,2023830,0,1,0,1,"2017-07-28T10:35:55","sanp","",[],"","Proof - why India is still a slave?","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2KNQrFW2O4c","politics"],[1,9982598,0,0,0,0,"2017-07-28T11:11:01","lemon11","",[],"<p>Yes, it's those evil businesses that try to bring jobs to India, employing thousands of people. Not the same reason they have &quot;socialist&quot; in their constitution, no.</p>"]]
[[0,2023831,0,90,1,89,"2017-07-28T10:36:19","killer7","",[],"","Metal smelting technology using primitive tools","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VVV4xeWBIxE","technology"],[1,9983343,0,10,0,10,"2017-07-28T13:19:16","scrimmmy","",[],"<p>This guy has a bunch of these videos, I believe. He made a really cool water hammer.</p>"],[2,9984060,9983343,5,0,5,"2017-07-28T14:41:50","Gravspeed","",[],"<p>It's really neat to watch him progress. He has made it into the iron age</p>"],[3,9984475,9984060,4,0,4,"2017-07-28T15:21:51","Awful-Falafel","",[],"<p>Just a matter of time until this guy gets to the nuclear age at the rate he's going.</p>"],[4,9984494,9984475,5,0,5,"2017-07-28T15:24:44","Gravspeed","",[],"<p>I think he has about the best shot at meeting Joe Rogan's challenge... If you went into the woods with a hatchet, how long would it take you to send me an email?</p>"],[2,9984077,9983343,2,0,2,"2017-07-28T14:43:42","Doomking_Grimlock","",[],"<p>He's made tons of cool stuff. I really liked his video on making charcoal, went through it step by step, showed you exactly what you needed to do. So simple and yet I doubt most people would have any idea how to even begin.</p>"],[1,9983519,0,5,0,5,"2017-07-28T13:44:33","Gringojones","",[],"<p>This guy is pretty awesome. I can watch these videos for hours. My assumption is that this is his thesis on primitive tools or something. </p>"],[2,9984089,9983519,1,0,1,"2017-07-28T14:44:24","Doomking_Grimlock","",[],"<p>I think he mentioned something to that effect in a video description or one of the comments.</p>"],[3,9984397,9984089,1,0,1,"2017-07-28T15:13:16","Gringojones","",[],"<p>That's awesome</p>"],[4,9984988,9984397,1,0,1,"2017-07-28T16:12:20","Doomking_Grimlock","",[],"<p>I know, right? I mean, how many students would go to that length for a thesis? The dude is brilliant.</p>"],[1,9983774,0,7,0,7,"2017-07-28T14:14:26","Jason_Argo","",[],"<p>this guy's channel is great, definitely check it out. no quick cuts or shitty techno playing in the background like 99% of youtube. A channel made for people with an attention span longer than 30 seconds I'm amazed it's as popular as it is.</p>"],[1,9984004,0,1,0,1,"2017-07-28T14:34:41","Laserchalk","",[],"<p>I like how he demonstrates how the design changes over time.</p>"],[1,9984673,0,5,0,5,"2017-07-28T15:41:23","Helios-Apollo","[e]",[],"<p>Just white people things. We're pretty awesome.</p>"],[1,9984700,0,1,0,1,"2017-07-28T15:44:50","grendelbiter","[e]",[],"<p>I love this guys channel. I'm trying to make a survival game in VR based on this guys stuff. I already got the axe: <a href=\"http://imgur.com/iaHkD8h\">http://imgur.com/iaHkD8h</a></p>\n<p>and the bow: <a href=\"http://imgur.com/iQIzbEn\">http://imgur.com/iQIzbEn</a></p>\n<p>I've been trying the past months to make an open world in VR. It's very tough, especially because I want very dense Jungle. The only way I can do it is if have no directional sunlight and use only ambient light. A pretty big drawback, but I hope that if the Jungle is dense enough it might not be as noticeable. </p>\n<p>I have a small demo scene with the bow set up for shooting. The arrows don't stick to anything yet and I know I need to adjust bow pull still. Here it is: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/lizz9ui6kgei5y3/StoneAgeVR.rar?dl=1\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/lizz9ui6kgei5y3/StoneAgeVR.rar?dl=1</a></p>\n<p>Edit: forgot to mention this is for Vive only.</p>"],[1,9985548,0,3,0,3,"2017-07-28T17:08:53","Itsdone63","",[],"<p>This is one of those time sinks that ends with you becoming an expert in steel forging.</p>"],[1,9986899,0,1,0,1,"2017-07-28T19:13:02","Holonomic","",[],"<p>What was the white powder/granules added near the end? Was that ground up shells, limestone? aka: CaCO3?</p>"],[1,9989637,0,3,0,3,"2017-07-28T23:57:28","hidflect","",[],"<p>I knew it. He started out with a straw hut and he's working his way up to mobile phone manufacturing.</p>"],[1,9992753,0,2,0,2,"2017-07-29T07:37:11","CrustyBeaver52","",[],"<p>Fuck - give him a month and he'll build an aircraft carrier - he's totally ruined Gilligan's Island.</p>"]]
[[0,2023832,0,2,0,2,"2017-07-28T10:36:49","Jack32","",[],"","Poll: Global Warming - Fact or Fiction!","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IkBlUnPbSY0","news"],[1,9982484,0,0,0,0,"2017-07-28T10:47:20","DoctorShitlord","",[],"<p>Fiction</p>"],[1,9982523,0,0,0,0,"2017-07-28T10:56:41","Engourgedilk","",[],"<p>Fact: If global warming is really such a bug deal, then why to a hand full of container ships produce the same if not <a href=\"http://www.industrytap.com/worlds-15-biggest-ships-create-more-pollution-than-all-the-cars-in-the-world/8182\">more</a> pollution as all the cars on the planet? Why not make those solar power and see if it gets cooler. Its essentially like removing half the cars from planet earth basically right? Fuck you, sad part is even if it is real... were all doomed to the apathy and dilution created by this miss information climate. </p>"],[2,9982626,9982523,0,0,0,"2017-07-28T11:16:16","MichaelCaine","",[],"<p>It would be a help. It will take lots of different acts to slow this down. </p>"],[2,9993036,9982523,0,0,0,"2017-07-29T08:59:33","Jack32","",[],"<p>Yeah, fuck you, your're damn right!</p>"]]
